A symbolic link to nothing named like a C header, in a directory that holds no
package, an editor's lock file, a link to nothing named like a C source, in a
package directory, and a link named like a C header through a file there. None
has content the build or a compiler can read, so the tree holds no non-Go source
and nothing is retained.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/dangling

go 1.27.0
-- docs/broken.h.symlink --
/nonexistent/target.h
-- p/p.go --
package p

var spare int

func Run() {}
-- p/.#p.c.symlink --
user@host.1234
-- p/a.h.symlink --
p.go/nothing.h
-- main.go --
package main

import "example.com/dangling/p"

func main() { p.Run() }
